From: Mirdispo contributors
Subject: Publish each stream's state on D-Bus under a name its client can find

A client that starts a stream learns its unit name and nothing else. Whether
the helper is still running has to be asked of systemd, or inside a Flatpak
sandbox of /proc, which only shows processes in the same sandbox instance.
Neither says whether the receiver is getting a picture yet. The helper does
know that, as its sink's state, but kept it to itself.

The daemon now hands the unit name to the helper as ND_STREAM_UNIT, through
the transient unit's Environment property or the child's environment. The
helper names itself <bus prefix>.Stream_<connection id>, taken from the unit
name, so the client can compute the name from what StartStream returned. The
helper publishes its sink's state (wait-p2p, wait-socket, wait-streaming,
streaming, ...) as the state of a "state" action, which GApplication exports
through org.gtk.Actions. A helper started without ND_STREAM_UNIT keeps the
random name it had before.

D-Bus names are seen by the whole session, so this works across sandbox
instances as well as outside a sandbox.

